WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.875
This episode focuses on program choice.

2
00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:12.187
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:12.187 --> 00:00:14.452
Start with a question, not a table.

4
00:00:14.452 --> 00:00:21.311
Define the people or organizations, measure, geography, and time period before selecting a Census program.

5
00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:30.370
Population counts, household characteristics, housing conditions, business activity, and government finance come from different collections.

6
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.558
Write the statistical universe in ordinary language.

7
00:00:33.558 --> 00:00:41.527
A value might describe residents, households, occupied housing units, workers, establishments with paid employees, or governments.

8
00:00:41.527 --> 00:00:47.963
A percentage without its denominator can answer a different question than the one a decision maker asked.

9
00:00:47.963 --> 00:00:53.666
Record the program, dataset, vintage, table or variable identifier, geography, and retrieval date.

10
00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:59.602
Keep survey estimates separate from administrative counts and preserve margins of error when supplied.

11
00:00:59.602 --> 00:01:01.581
The record is part of the finding.

12
00:01:01.581 --> 00:01:03.327
Torrance application segment.

13
00:01:03.327 --> 00:01:07.601
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

14
00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:15.246
The cited City of Torrance primary source is About Torrance, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/About-Torrance.

15
00:01:15.246 --> 00:01:23.133
For a local analysis, use the City's baseline facts to frame a question, then select the federal program that actually measures it.

16
00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:31.621
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

17
00:01:31.621 --> 00:01:41.591
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

18
00:01:41.591 --> 00:01:44.833
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

19
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:49.604
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

20
00:01:49.604 --> 00:01:53.885
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

21
00:01:53.885 --> 00:01:59.879
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

22
00:01:59.879 --> 00:02:04.222
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
